  "articleBody": "Uneven walls can be a real headache when you're trying to get those baseboards looking just right. It's not uncommon, especially in older homes, to find walls that aren't perfectly straight or floors that aren't quite level. This can lead to unsightly gaps, poor corner joints, and baseboards that just don't sit flush. A common mistake is trying to force the baseboard into place or relying heavily on caulk to hide the imperfections. While caulk can help with minor gaps, it's not a substitute for a good fit, and it can actually highlight bigger issues over time. Instead, you need to consider how to prepare your walls and how to make strategic cuts to accommodate these variations. Sometimes, it involves a bit of shimming behind the baseboard or even some minor wall repair. The key is to address the underlying unevenness rather than just covering it up. If you're encountering significant variations or if you want that truly seamless, built-in look, that's often when bringing in a professional like HH Remodeling LLC makes a lot of sense. We've got the tools and the know-how to tackle those tricky situations and make sure your baseboards look fantastic, even in less-than-perfect rooms. Don't let a wonky wall ruin your renovation; get it done right the first time.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
